then direct children, then deeper entries, exactly one divider"},{"forClaim":6,"rationale":"Records the intended outcome for the weakest-tier app against the strongest-tier menu entry, so the cross-tier bias is a deliberate, tested guarantee.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":376}],"title":"searchScore: description-only app match vs exact-label menu entry"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #12223 (Menu.qml, MenuModel.js, menu-test.sh) puts installed apps above menu entries in search. (1) searchScore's app bias goes from a within-tier -5 to -100, larger than every tier, so any matching app outranks any menu entry (`vsc` -> VS Code above the VSCode menu entries). (2) At the root, matching app rows are listed before direct-child matches. By design this replaces the old guarantee that a better-matching menu entry beats a weaker app (`font`). Routing is unchanged. Dogfood-only parts: the re-extracted replay mirror test/node/menumodel-replay.test.mjs and review/ notes (not in upstream).\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Part 1: the changed MenuModel.js decision line is measured and covered (0 uncovered lines or outcomes). Part 2 is QML: no coverage measures it and no test runs it. It is only regex-matched in source. The package records no observed test outcomes (test_outcome_unobserved), so this review makes no pass claims.\n\n**Questions for a human.** Can a root search with apps, direct children and deeper matches show the right order and exactly one divider (the current/deeper divider disappears when apps match)? Should an app that matches only by description beat a menu entry whose label is exactly the query?\n\n**Traceability.** SW-REQ-260922-SJ7P (\"apps demote by 5 within a tier\") and SW-REQ-260922-TKDP (\"current-menu matches before deeper\") now contradict the code. The spec is out of date, not the code; amend both in this change. SYS-REQ-260922-V7W6's \"match quality\" needs a note. The other changed requirements match only at file level.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** Readiness is blocked (pre_existing_only): all 28 blocking disclosures (18 failed checks, 10 missing obligations) held at baseline ce925cb1 (every gate delta unchanged). Next decision: investigation, authority change_author."}
